  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The solid circle uses twelve "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "treble"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "treble"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " increases per round rather than six, because trebles stand taller than double crochet and need more circumference added per round to stay flat. Unlike the flat double crochet circle, the increases do not stagger; they land in the same column each round, which can produce a slight scallop at the outer edge. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "blocking"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Blocking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " corrects this. Three rounds give a 10 cm disc that is thick enough to use as a coaster or pot holder."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "variant": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK weight cotton, approximately 22 m per motif. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors, stitch marker (optional), blocking mat and pins."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "3 rounds in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook = 10 cm diameter after blocking. Trebles are taller than double crochet, so the disc grows quickly per round. If you need a larger circle, simply add more rounds following the same 12-increase-per-round rule."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
