          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Work 2 tr in each st around. Join with sl st to top of ch 3. (24 tr.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 3"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ch 3 (counts as first tr). *2 tr in next st, 1 tr in next st*; repeat from * to * around. Join with sl st to top of ch 3. Fasten off. (36 tr.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "craftChart",
        "attrs": {
          "slug": "crochet-motif-solid-circle"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in tails. Wet-block by soaking the motif in cold water, pressing out moisture gently, then pinning flat to a blocking mat. If the edge scallops, pin between each increase point to stretch the edge into a smooth curve. Leave to dry fully before unpinning."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solid circles join most neatly with a mattress stitch or back-stitch seam worked through the outer edge stitches. Because the edge is dense (treble tops), there is no need for a special joining round; the stitch tops provide a clean surface for seaming."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine wash at 30 °C on a gentle cycle or hand wash in cool water. Lay flat to dry. Block again if needed."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The spiral round motif removes the join step for a seamless look, while the shell round motif adds a decorative shell edging to the outer round of this same disc."
          }
        ]
      }
